  {
   "control_type": "Text",
   "name": "BugReportingBanner.png\n\nA report containing crash information has been generated. To submit crash data for bug tracking only, send the following zipped file to $Link *crashes@ableton.com* <mailto:crashes@ableton.com>:\n\n$Link Ableton Crash Report 2026-08-08 004023 Live 12.1.zip<reveal:C:\\Users\\DELL\\AppData\\Roaming\\Ableton\\Live Reports\\Ableton Crash Report 2026-08-08 004023 Live 12.1.zip>\n\nTo look for the cause of the crash, follow the steps in the $Link Troubleshooting a crash <https://help.ableton.com/hc/articles/209773265> guide, or visit the $Link Ableton Knowledge Base <https://help.ableton.com/hc/> for more help topics.\n\nNote: *Crash Reports* submitted to crashes@ableton.com are not sent to the Ableton Support team and will not receive a reply. To request technical support, visit $Link https://www.ableton.com/help/#contact-support <https://www.ableton.com/help/#contact-support>. Please include a description of the crash and the *zipped* crash report with your request.\n\nDivider.tif\n\nThe crash report encloses copies of the following folders on your computer:\n\n-> Live's current *Preferences, Unlock* and *UsageData* folders\n-> Crash logs created by the operating system *(Mac)* or by Live *(Win),* if available\n\nFor more information, visit $Link Where to find Crash Reports <https://help.ableton.com/hc/en-us/articles/209071629-Where-to-find-Crash-Reports>. Data in the report is used exclusively to track and fix issues. To learn how your information may be used, see our $Link privacy policy <https://www.ableton.com/privacy-policy>.\n\nDivider.tif\n\nThank you for taking the time to report a crash.",
